# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings, on every
# OS, whatever core.autocrlf says. Tools that edit text then never have to
# reproduce CRLF, which is how stray \r escapes got into the registry in
# slice 4 (architecture review F4, Micah 2026-10-09). Binary files (the
# AISC workbook, PDFs) are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
